# ============================================
# IMPORTANT: K3s WILL REVERT THIS ON RESTART
# ============================================
# K3s's CoreDNS addon manager re-applies the bundled Corefile every time
# the CoreDNS pods are recreated. So this fix only survives pod restarts,
# NOT k3s restarts or WSL reboots.
#
# To make it persistent, you have TWO options:
#
# Option A: Re-apply this script every time after k3s restart
#   (run `bash scripts/fixes/apply-coredns.sh` in your rc.local)
#
# Option B: Use k3s auto-deploy (preferred)
#   Copy config/k3s/coredns-rewrite-autodeploy.yaml to
#   /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/manifests/ on the WSL server
#   k3s will auto-apply it on every boot
#
# We use Option B in production setup.
